{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520995-would-that-make-a-good-idea-for-a-fangame","id":1520995,"title":"Would that make a good idea for a fangame?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-19T17:04:00-07:00","id":1520995,"title":"Would that make a good idea for a fangame?","content":"so,at the present moment,i don't have time and energy to make a fangame but I'm still blessed and cursed with ideas for them,all of the ideas are fun but only few would truly work.<br /> One I'm particularly proud of is a fangame where protagonists are &quot;Heralds of Doomsday&quot;<br /> Have you ever noticed how every doomsday prophecy has a herald,Ragnarok has one,So does the Christian Apocalypse. There's always an angel blowing an horn or rooster crowing to announce the End of Days<br /> What if you played them?<br /> In this gameline you'd play people cursed with a state that makes their very existence a beacon for disaster,they'd settle in a place and a hurricane/plague/bombing/whatever would happen<br /> their powers would include learning to channeling their curse to hurt their enemies and manipulate fate<br /> their societies would include several different views on what is their place on the world,should they embrace their curse? deny it? try to find a balance<br /> wouldn't that make a fun fangame?<br /> <br /> P.S If you wanna take the idea and develop yourself,feel free to do so. just remember to credit me as the one who came up with it<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T12:53:54-07:00","id":1521054,"title":"","content":"Certainly seems interesting. I don't think I'd be able to take it up myself, but I'm willing to provide moral support for anyone who does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T20:58:57-07:00","id":1521097,"title":"","content":"Harbingers. Fated to speak the end of the world, but they turned away from that fate (for a reason based on their splat). The stronger they grow, the more terrible the disasters that follow in their wake. <br /> <br /> Another possible inspiration: Mothman, who was apparently seen before several large-scale disasters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T02:52:06-07:00","id":1521111,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;Harbingers: the armaggedom&quot; was a title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T10:23:13-07:00","id":1521136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520995-would-that-make-a-good-idea-for-a-fangame?p=1521097#post1521097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harbingers. Fated to speak the end of the world, but they turned away from that fate (for a reason based on their splat). The stronger they grow, the more terrible the disasters that follow in their wake.<br /> <br /> Another possible inspiration: Mothman, who was apparently seen before several large-scale disasters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hooo, nice description-summary there! Mothman could easily be an interesting inspiration, alongside his/its more avian \u2018cousin\u2019; <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=iNXRkjzKb-8\" target=\"_blank\">the Blackbird of Chernobyl</a>. Heck, one power that Harbingers could have/obtain/unlock is the ability to assume a (partially?) bestial form that provides benefits that scale with their Power Stat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520995-would-that-make-a-good-idea-for-a-fangame?p=1521111#post1521111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about &quot;Harbingers: the armaggedom&quot; was a title?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems as good as any. I say we stick with it until we agree on something more suitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T03:36:35-07:00","id":1521176,"title":"","content":"Would it have to be a disaster? Multiple events could be fated to happen, also how would the campaign process once the event occurs? Would having the type of event characters herald change or should that remain consistent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T13:03:57-07:00","id":1521215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520995-would-that-make-a-good-idea-for-a-fangame?p=1521176#post1521176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it have to be a disaster? Multiple events could be fated to happen, also how would the campaign process once the event occurs? Would having the type of event characters herald change or should that remain consistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe one Axis could be a general type of disaster, and so long as it stays within that type, a Harbinger could call down pretty much any apocalyptic event that's within their power to do so. Kinda' like how the 'Family' X-Splat of Beast indicated what sort of Nightmare their Horror was spawned from; near-infinite variety, limited theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T13:09:51-07:00","id":1521217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520995-would-that-make-a-good-idea-for-a-fangame?p=1521215#post1521215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe one Axis could be a general type of disaster, and so long as it stays within that type, a Harbinger could call down pretty much any apocalyptic event that's within their power to do so. Kinda' like how the 'Family' X-Splat of Beast indicated what sort of Nightmare their Horror was spawned from; near-infinite variety, limited theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>ooh I like that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T18:08:23-07:00","id":1521229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520995-would-that-make-a-good-idea-for-a-fangame#post1520995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so,at the present moment,i don't have time and energy to make a fangame but I'm still blessed and cursed with ideas for them,all of the ideas are fun but only few would truly work.<br /> One I'm particularly proud of is a fangame where protagonists are &quot;Heralds of Doomsday&quot;<br /> Have you ever noticed how every doomsday prophecy has a herald,Ragnarok has one,So does the Christian Apocalypse. There's always an angel blowing an horn or rooster crowing to announce the End of Days<br /> What if you played them?<br /> In this gameline you'd play people cursed with a state that makes their very existence a beacon for disaster,they'd settle in a place and a hurricane/plague/bombing/whatever would happen<br /> their powers would include learning to channeling their curse to hurt their enemies and manipulate fate<br /> their societies would include several different views on what is their place on the world,should they embrace their curse? deny it? try to find a balance<br /> wouldn't that make a fun fangame?<br /> <br /> P.S If you wanna take the idea and develop yourself,feel free to do so. just remember to credit me as the one who came up with it</div> </div> </div> </div>So.<br /> <br /> 1) I think this is just a tweak of direction away from Oracle: the Endbringers, and<br /> 2) No, this is not substantial enough for a Noun: the Gerund gameline. Maybe something smaller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T04:37:16-07:00","id":1521247,"title":"","content":"I suggest Harbinger: The Fated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],